{"kind":"assert","text":"Step 5 of the repository discipline cannot produce a merge artifact that is not stale from birth, demonstrated twice today by following it exactly. Merge artifact a5ef7fe2f2d92974f75f3233c139593fce4cfc33 for the write-time unreadable-kind warning, and cefec14de9954bc48837a9b0b9ddd8dc98d861ea for the bounded stale-commitment qualifier, both project stale with describes_superseded_world set, within seconds of being filed. The chain is short and forced: the merge artifact rests on the ratified approval report, the report rests on its promise, the promise on the review request, and the review request on the pre-merge branch artifact. Step 5 requires superseding that branch artifact for the same path in the same step. Retiring it flares everything resting on it, so the artifact recording the merged state inherits staleness from the predecessor it was required to retire. Doing the ceremony correctly is what makes the record wrong. This is the case proposal f9f077ba names in the abstract: a rests_on that records what an act was made in light of is being read as a claim about a world that must still hold. Forty-nine of three hundred live artifacts now carry stale."}